  "description": "Built for attacking the toughest descents, but also designed for comfort, stability and speed on long, fast fire roads, the MYLC is a totally unique bike – perhaps the only mass-produced gravel bike with such radical geometry. We designed it in complete isolation from the road and cyclocross trends on which almost every other gravel bike is based. Instead, we looked at the terrain gravel bikes actually live on and took our cues from mountain bikes: ultra long reach and a slack head angle. Contrary to popular belief, long bikes with slack head angles are not slow. A stable bike lets you focus on pedaling and generating power instead of fighting a bouncing front end, so you get less tired and go further. The cobblestone roads you used to hate become segments you pedal smoothly in the saddle, and the descents that used to scare you turn out to be quite accessible.\n\nLike all RONDO bikes, the MYLC is fitted with the TwinTip fork – a unique feature that allows you to fine tune the handling and set up your bike exactly the way you like. Use the \"HI\" position if you prefer the feeling of a more dynamic, fast turning road bike and switch it to \"LO\" to get the stability that comes from a more relaxed, MTB-inspired front end.\n\nThe latest MYLC carbon frame keeps the Enhanced Gravel Geometry (EGG) – significantly longer reach and a slacker head tube angle – and adds everything a modern gravel bike needs: a UDH derailleur hanger, a threaded T47 bottom bracket, fully internal cable routing through the headset, and a short seat tube with low standover that leaves room for a dropper post. The frame itself is designed to soak up vibrations, so high speed on bumpy roads stays under control.\n\nThe MYLC MX1 is the most extreme version in the family and the epitome of a no-limits gravel bike. At its heart is a mullet drivetrain: wireless SRAM Rival AXS levers with new, more ergonomic hoods up front and SRAM's Eagle AXS Transmission at the back. The full mount derailleur bolts straight to the frame – no hanger to bend, no limit screws to fiddle with – and the 10–52 cassette gives you a climbing gear straight from a mountain bike. A dropper post drops the saddle out of the way when the trail points down, the wide-flare RONDO FLARE 2 bar gives you leverage in the drops, and WTB Raddler tires – fast in the center, aggressive on the edges – bite into loose corners. Reynolds G30 wheels with a lifetime guarantee take the hits. Sand and black, made for dust. If you want to ride a bike from the future today, try the MYLC!",
